>> title: Ham Hock Stock
>> category: Soups
>> tags: pork, stock, southern, smoked, make-ahead
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: smoked pork stock, ham hock broth, smoked pork pot, seasoning meat, pot likker base, smoked turkey stock
>> servings: 12
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — salt stays out until the end: the hocks are already salty, and everything built on this stock inherits it
>> pairs-with: collard-greens, green-beans, black-eyed-peas, butter-beans

>> step: Cook this once and four sides come out of it, so it is worth three quarts at a time.
Cook this once and four sides come out of it.

>> step: rinse, into the pot
Rinse @smoked ham hocks{2}(about 2 lb / 900 g), @smoked pork neck bones{1%lb}(450 g) and lay them in a #stockpot{}.

>> step: simmer bare 3 hr, skimmed
Simmer @&(~1)smoked pork{} with @cold water{4%qt}(3.8 L), @yellow onion{1%large}(halved), @garlic{6%cloves}(smashed), @bay leaves{2}, @black peppercorns{1%tsp}, @dried red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp} at a bare ~simmer{3%hr}, skimming the grey foam off in the first ten minutes.

>> step: strain, pick the meat off the bone
Strain @&(~1)pot{} through a #fine sieve{} and pick the meat off the bone.

Stir the picked meat back into whichever pot this stock goes into.
